Package: tokr
Type: Package
Title: Plain-Text Information-Process Models in tok (BPMN 2.0, DMN, Forms)
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: person("Marek", "Deja", email = "marek.deja@uj.edu.pl", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Reads, checks, formats and exports process models written in tok,
    a plain-text language for BPMN 2.0 processes with decision tables (DMN),
    Camunda forms and simulation parameters. Models are checked against the
    BPMN 2.0 rules with diagnostics in English or Polish, exported to BPMN XML
    with diagram layout, SVG pictures, DMN and form files, and drawn in the
    viewer or in R Markdown and Quarto documents through a knitr engine.
    Processes are simulated as discrete-event models, giving indicators, an
    event log for process mining and a table of cases. The work is done by
    the Rust engine of tok, shared with the Python package.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://codeberg.org/MarekDeja/tok
BugReports: https://codeberg.org/MarekDeja/tok/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Suggests: knitr, rmarkdown, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.99
